                        "glosses": [
                            "Inferior poetry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a17cdac3-a8d6-405e-b076-e2afcf99aa81",
                                "sense_id": "dc55073e-bfd3-39ce-a445-e31b6e69101b",
                                "text": "As Poetry is totally distinct from Poetastery, so is Criticism not to be confounded with Criticastricism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82287e0e-d778-4c9f-bbf6-3f844a870a30",
                                "sense_id": "dc55073e-bfd3-39ce-a445-e31b6e69101b",
                                "text": "We rarely sentimentalized consciously, and still more seldom openly, about the present state of Venice as contrasted with her past glory. I am glad to say that we despised the conventional poetastery about her."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57a8f6b7-ef34-4d32-931b-917f5705fdc0",
                                "sense_id": "dc55073e-bfd3-39ce-a445-e31b6e69101b",
                                "text": "Compare but the northern poets — and they were all improvisers — with the lamentable poetastery of the Roman emperors which Suetonius quotes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
